    "blurb": "The Shoreline show delivers energetic first‑set highlights like Cold Rain And Snow and Stagger Lee, while the second set shines on Estimated Prophet and The Wheel. Recording quality is unusually clear for an audience tape, making it a reliable listen.",
    "review": "Shoreline Amphitheatre on September 16, 1994 offers a dependable Grateful Dead performance that leans into the band's mid‑'90s strengths. The first set bursts open with a crisp rendition of Cold Rain And Snow and rides through a lively Stagger Lee before slipping into a breezy Cassidy. The second set builds momentum with Victim Or The Crime, then launches into a soaring Estimated Prophet that segues into an expansive Eyes Of The World, eventually delivering a warm‑hearted Wheel that lands just before the upbeat Good Lovin'. A brief encore of Liberty caps off the night. While reviewers note the show stays solid throughout, some feel the flow dips after If The Shoe Fits, but overall the setlist sustains its groove. The audience recording (gd94-09-16.akg.seff.2642.sbeok.shnf) is praised for being unusually clear and free of major drop‑outs, providing a surprisingly detailed capture of this solid ’94 outing.\n\nGiven the limited commentary on individual members—Jerry receives a passing nod but no specific praise—the band’s collective performance feels competent and true to form rather than extraordinary. Fans looking for an accessible snapshot of the 1994 era will find this tape both enjoyable and historically useful.",
